WEBVTT

00:02.410 --> 00:05.380
In matters relating
to the world of the dead

00:05.480 --> 00:08.840
there is an institution that judges
the sins of the deceased

00:09.100 --> 00:10.640
the Ju-Oh-Cho.

00:11.480 --> 00:13.250
The Summons Section
of the Judgment Bureau

00:13.350 --> 00:17.080
comprises a group supporting
the ministry's operating functions

00:17.190 --> 00:20.020
by guiding the lost souls
that wander the mortal world.

00:20.390 --> 00:22.020
They are also known as...

00:22.260 --> 00:24.700
the Shinigami.

00:24.960 --> 00:31.630
nureta hitomi no oku

00:24.960 --> 00:31.630
Deep behind its wavering stare

00:33.340 --> 00:43.650
aoi tsuki wa shizuka ni koboreochiteyuku

00:33.340 --> 00:43.650
The pale moon quietly descends

00:33.520 --> 00:42.770
Yami no Matsuei

00:49.960 --> 00:55.830
azayaka na sekai wa

00:49.960 --> 00:55.830
The splendid world

00:58.200 --> 01:08.270
oto mo naku shizuka ni yami ni kieteyuku

00:58.200 --> 01:08.270
Disappears into the darkness without a sound

01:08.370 --> 01:16.010
byouyomi no naka kakemeguru yami no naka o

01:08.370 --> 01:16.010
Running about in the dark as time runs out

01:16.110 --> 01:22.640
soshite aratanaru toki o mukae ima

01:16.110 --> 01:22.640
A new era beckons now

01:25.360 --> 01:30.450
kizutsuita kuroi tsubasa

01:25.360 --> 01:30.450
The injured black wings

01:30.630 --> 01:37.000
tsuki no akari ni terasarete

01:30.630 --> 01:37.000
Shine in the moonlight

01:37.600 --> 01:41.800
utsukushiku maiagare

01:37.600 --> 01:41.800
Rising upward in a beautiful dance

01:41.940 --> 01:47.140
shinku no kuchizuke ga ima

01:41.940 --> 01:47.140
The crimson kiss

01:47.250 --> 01:54.080
kokoro no oku ni nagarekomu

01:47.250 --> 01:54.080
Flows deeply into the soul

01:54.250 --> 02:00.050
soshite yume no naka e

01:54.250 --> 02:00.050
Penetrating into one's dreams

02:14.340 --> 02:16.330
The land that is Kyoto...

02:16.440 --> 02:20.070
is a place with quite a strong spirit energy.

02:20.980 --> 02:23.210
Personally, I find it...

02:23.310 --> 02:26.310
I find the energy at Sagano to be comforting.

02:26.420 --> 02:28.040
Comforting, you say.

02:28.150 --> 02:30.240
That's something
I should be worried about.

02:30.350 --> 02:32.150
Whenever you come here

02:32.260 --> 02:35.160
it's only because of some sinister plan you have.

02:35.790 --> 02:38.350
Oriya, I have a favor to ask.

02:41.000 --> 02:42.060
A card key?

02:42.170 --> 02:44.830
When the Shinigami come after me

02:44.930 --> 02:46.900
use this as a decoy and stall them.

02:47.300 --> 02:51.210
Even if only for a minute or a second.

02:52.640 --> 02:54.130
Don't worry.

02:54.340 --> 02:56.370
I won't cause you any more trouble after this.

02:56.480 --> 02:58.570
Don't, Muraki.

02:58.780 --> 03:02.080
When all of this is over, I will disappear.

03:03.020 --> 03:05.540
Stop this!
Don't talk like this is the end!

03:05.760 --> 03:09.820
Why do you always have to be like this?!

03:10.160 --> 03:11.720
Why...?!

03:13.300 --> 03:15.130
I have no choice.

03:15.230 --> 03:19.130
I've been programmed like
this ever since that day.

03:19.770 --> 03:22.200
This is what I am.

03:27.780 --> 03:30.750
Well, I'll be counting on you.

03:37.630 --> 03:42.590
Episode 13: The Kyoto Arc, Part 4

03:46.200 --> 03:48.460
- Drowning?
- Yeah, I hear it's a drowning.

03:48.570 --> 03:50.620
He was a college professor?

03:50.730 --> 03:54.670
Things are pretty ugly with
suicides and serial murders.

03:57.870 --> 04:01.780
And he was our only witness
relating to these incidents.

04:01.880 --> 04:04.470
He's not coming back anymore.

04:05.320 --> 04:09.310
Tsuzuki didn't want to hurt anyone anymore.

04:12.920 --> 04:16.590
But, in the end, he gave priority to his own life.

04:16.830 --> 04:18.660
He despaired over himself

04:18.760 --> 04:21.530
and buried himself in a deep darkness.

04:22.470 --> 04:26.160
I doubt that Tsuzuki will ever return.

04:26.270 --> 04:28.360
Keep your wits about yourself, Kurosaki-kun!

04:28.470 --> 04:31.030
If you, as his partner, are going to say that

04:31.140 --> 04:33.540
we'll never be able to
get him back from Muraki!

04:33.640 --> 04:36.510
But, even if we were able to save him

04:36.610 --> 04:39.410
he might not be able to be his self again.

04:39.850 --> 04:43.050
To me, or to everyone else...

04:43.390 --> 04:47.290
He'll probably have forgotten everything.

04:47.720 --> 04:51.020
It's not as though we've forgotten him.

04:51.930 --> 04:56.460
As long as we remember him,
he will continue to exist.

04:56.770 --> 05:00.400
His existence is certainly
not reduced to zero, Kurosaki-kun.

05:03.040 --> 05:04.970
Not reduced to zero...

05:06.580 --> 05:08.980
Let's go!
We have to save Tsuzuki!

05:12.950 --> 05:16.350
We checked out every hotel in the city

05:16.450 --> 05:18.650
but Muraki's name didn't come up.

05:19.020 --> 05:23.430
But then again, he wouldn't
use his real name anyway.

05:23.530 --> 05:27.460
And, on the outside, this is a
high-class establishment for VIP's.

05:27.660 --> 05:30.000
But it's actually a house of prostitution.

05:30.100 --> 05:32.930
Moreover, the young master in charge of here...

05:33.040 --> 05:35.970
I hear was an old high school friend of Muraki's.

05:36.070 --> 05:39.440
I see.
A perfect place to hide.

05:49.250 --> 05:50.980
Welcome to Kokakurou

05:51.090 --> 05:53.450
my dear Shinigami from the land beyond.

05:53.560 --> 05:55.620
Tell us! Where's Muraki?!

05:55.730 --> 05:58.090
Don't throw a hissy fit.

05:58.190 --> 06:00.890
Muraki's in the basement at the university.

06:01.000 --> 06:04.630
Probably with that guy you're looking for.

06:05.300 --> 06:06.670
Hold it!

06:06.770 --> 06:09.800
He's probably set up an energy
shield in the basement there.

06:09.910 --> 06:13.070
So you won't be able to get
past it even in spirit form.

06:13.180 --> 06:16.300
You'll need this in order to get in there.

06:24.390 --> 06:27.290
Our swords are brothers of the same mold.

06:27.390 --> 06:30.790
It is only through your
strength that you can win.

06:30.890 --> 06:33.120
I will not lose!

06:33.900 --> 06:35.020
I see.

06:35.400 --> 06:38.130
I can't let myself lose as well.

06:38.230 --> 06:41.070
He made me a promise after all.

06:41.470 --> 06:42.440
Kid...

06:42.570 --> 06:46.030
I suppose we'll see whose will is stronger.

06:48.140 --> 06:50.310
You going to be all right, kid?

06:50.750 --> 06:54.010
Only Kurosaki-kun has a particular
interest in the martial arts.

06:54.120 --> 06:57.090
We'll just have to rely on him.

07:08.330 --> 07:09.920
Grandfather...

07:10.130 --> 07:13.000
I have brought your patient back to you.

07:16.870 --> 07:20.830
I've waited...
I've waited so long...

07:21.280 --> 07:22.840
for this moment.

07:27.750 --> 07:31.280
Did you have a bad dream, Tsuzuki-san?

07:32.420 --> 07:34.520
Don't worry.

07:34.890 --> 07:38.090
You will soon never dream again.

07:41.560 --> 07:44.190
Kid, what are you fighting for?!

07:44.300 --> 07:46.030
Is it to bring back your friend?

07:46.470 --> 07:48.840
Or is it simply out of hate for Muraki?

07:48.940 --> 07:50.930
Is this the power of hate?!

07:54.510 --> 07:56.640
You'll never beat him.

07:58.250 --> 07:59.870
Kurosaki-kun!

08:00.350 --> 08:01.940
That settles it.

08:04.350 --> 08:05.650
Hold it...

08:06.460 --> 08:07.950
- Kid!
- Kurosaki-kun!

08:08.060 --> 08:10.650
That guy's a pretty tough one to beat.

08:10.760 --> 08:14.990
Tsuzuki has saved me many times before.

08:15.670 --> 08:18.330
When I was so mistrustful of people...

08:18.430 --> 08:22.340
and so closed in spirit after my death...

08:22.540 --> 08:26.840
he gently and calmly
gave me love and warmth.

08:27.280 --> 08:30.840
He always protected me with his smile!

08:31.850 --> 08:36.110
If Tsuzuki is in trouble, I want to save him!

08:39.460 --> 08:43.790
This time I want to be his strength!

08:44.730 --> 08:47.860
I see you like a good gamble, kid.

08:48.230 --> 08:51.430
I like that.
I'll accept your determination!

08:55.040 --> 08:57.870
<i>The place that I finally found...</i>

08:57.970 --> 09:02.340
<i>Watari-san, Tatsumi-san and
everyone at the Summons Bureau...</i>

09:03.210 --> 09:05.810
<i>A warm place, like being a part of a family.</i>

09:07.980 --> 09:10.980
<i>But that's because Tsuzuki led me there.</i>

09:12.220 --> 09:16.180
<i>It was because he was there,
that I was able to exist in that place.</i>

09:18.900 --> 09:22.520
<i>I will fight in order to save Tsuzuki.</i>

09:22.730 --> 09:24.530
<i>His doubts have ceased!</i>

09:26.500 --> 09:27.530
Come!

09:50.760 --> 09:53.060
You win.

09:53.260 --> 09:54.560
What're you talking about?!

09:54.660 --> 09:59.000
Take your sword!
I have to defeat you!

09:59.100 --> 10:02.130
I have to get Tsuzuki back!

10:02.240 --> 10:03.570
Kid...

10:03.670 --> 10:07.170
Even a violent man has one reason or another.

10:07.840 --> 10:13.010
Even he is fighting for the same reason as you.

10:18.750 --> 10:22.450
A man like me, living in my
ghostly world, has no right

10:22.560 --> 10:26.150
to interfere with the two
who are fighting for their lives.

10:26.900 --> 10:29.230
Hurry up and go save your friend.

10:29.330 --> 10:33.290
And go get back your place in the world.

10:41.580 --> 10:44.600
Did I do the right thing?

10:46.750 --> 10:49.550
Don't you die, Muraki.

10:55.260 --> 10:57.730
I shall start the experiment.

10:57.830 --> 11:02.160
I shall transplant Saki's body to you.

11:02.800 --> 11:07.060
It should be possible
given your immortal ability.

11:18.010 --> 11:22.550
Yami no Matsuei

11:34.800 --> 11:36.560
<i>What are you doing?</i>

11:36.670 --> 11:38.190
<i>Taking care of the flowers.</i>

11:38.300 --> 11:41.290
<i>If you want to grow big, beautiful flowers</i>

11:41.400 --> 11:45.470
<i>you have to trim the buds.
That's basic for growing roses.</i>

11:45.570 --> 11:48.700
<i>But there's something sad about that.</i>

11:48.810 --> 11:51.370
<i>It's a life it worked so hard for.</i>

11:52.650 --> 11:57.020
<i>Isn't it too late for such sentiments, Asato?</i>

11:57.490 --> 11:59.350
<i>You are a murderer.</i>

11:59.460 --> 12:02.750
<i>You killed people like I did to these roses.</i>

12:02.860 --> 12:04.090
<i>You're wrong! I was...</i>

12:04.190 --> 12:07.560
<i>Then, what's all that behind you?</i>

12:11.530 --> 12:12.930
<i>No.</i>

12:13.040 --> 12:14.970
<i>I didn't want to kill her!</i>

12:31.550 --> 12:33.850
T-Tsuzuki-san...

12:39.860 --> 12:42.830
I wasn't supposed to exist.

12:42.930 --> 12:44.960
I shouldn't have been.

12:45.070 --> 12:48.470
Muraki, let's go together.

12:49.770 --> 12:52.710
You actually want to die with me?

12:54.580 --> 12:57.980
The flames of dark anger...

12:58.080 --> 13:01.880
take the form of a heavenly
serpent and descend upon me.

13:04.220 --> 13:08.090
Tsuzuki-san, even if you were to kill me

13:08.190 --> 13:11.790
that sorrow of yours will never be lifted.

13:12.190 --> 13:13.990
Come to me, Touda.

13:14.200 --> 13:19.160
Dark chaos, bring darkness to
the one who had been granted life.

13:21.540 --> 13:23.510
You cannot escape it.

13:23.610 --> 13:27.170
Both you and I are
the Descendants of Darkness!

13:34.720 --> 13:36.180
This is...

13:36.950 --> 13:38.680
Touda's flames?

13:42.890 --> 13:44.880
It's cold.

13:45.390 --> 13:49.350
My consciousness is slipping away.
Is this death?

13:50.930 --> 13:53.700
What an overdone ending to one's life.

13:55.470 --> 13:59.870
I can't just let it end like this.

14:01.580 --> 14:03.980
I cannot die yet.

14:06.750 --> 14:07.940
Saki!

14:08.050 --> 14:12.010
I will not die until I kill you
with my own two hands!

14:23.570 --> 14:26.090
Well, there's not much we can do with this.

14:26.200 --> 14:29.170
Don't be so negative!
Let's just go and get Tsuzuki!

14:30.070 --> 14:31.330
Tsuzuki...

14:32.810 --> 14:34.830
- Tsuzuki!
- Hold it, kid!

14:36.110 --> 14:38.440
The flames of Touda ain't no joke.

14:38.550 --> 14:40.910
It can overwhelm a
Shinigami's ability to recover.

14:41.020 --> 14:43.310
Even our lives are in danger!

14:43.420 --> 14:45.980
- Then, what about Tsuzuki?!
- He's used...

14:46.860 --> 14:51.520
He summoned Touda knowing
full well what he was doing.

14:51.630 --> 14:55.120
To make sure that he would die.

14:55.300 --> 14:58.430
- That's his wish.
- I don't believe that!

14:58.730 --> 15:01.930
I don't want to let Tsuzuki die.

15:02.040 --> 15:03.230
Kurosaki-kun...

15:03.340 --> 15:05.860
Even if that's what he really wants...

15:06.110 --> 15:07.870
I'll never accept that!

15:11.150 --> 15:12.210
Look.

15:12.850 --> 15:16.980
It's not a bad thing to respect people's wishes.

15:17.190 --> 15:18.350
Then again...

15:18.450 --> 15:23.390
it's not a bad thing to overrule
those wishes as well, Tatsumi.

15:26.000 --> 15:27.290
I suppose you're right.

15:30.070 --> 15:35.560
How many people have meaninglessly
died because they knew me?

15:36.170 --> 15:40.970
I'm probably one who ought
not to exist in this world.

15:57.460 --> 16:00.860
Burn more furiously, Touda.

16:00.960 --> 16:04.190
Burn everything away.

16:05.070 --> 16:07.540
And my immortal life.

16:09.810 --> 16:11.640
Tsuzuki!

16:12.470 --> 16:14.810
What are you doing?!
Come over here!

16:15.680 --> 16:16.910
Hisoka?

16:19.780 --> 16:22.880
Can't you move?
I'll go over there now!

16:25.290 --> 16:26.910
Tsuzuki, let's go!

16:28.820 --> 16:30.380
Tsuzuki?

16:30.490 --> 16:33.760
It's all right now, Hisoka.

16:34.160 --> 16:38.260
I've lived plenty long enough.

16:38.800 --> 16:41.200
I'm tired.

16:43.440 --> 16:46.770
I'm not supposed to exist.

16:47.310 --> 16:49.610
That's why I'm going to...

16:50.050 --> 16:51.310
Hisoka...?

16:51.410 --> 16:54.250
I want you to exist even just for me!

16:54.350 --> 16:56.580
I don't want to be left alone!

16:58.450 --> 17:01.220
This is the only place for me.

17:02.290 --> 17:06.520
Just here in your heart...!

17:11.600 --> 17:16.900
Is it all right for me to be here?

17:57.740 --> 18:00.200
Kokakurou

18:13.100 --> 18:15.120
He's gone.

18:23.070 --> 18:26.040
Konoe, how are Tsuzuki and Hisoka doing?

18:26.140 --> 18:28.670
Yes. Just before they vanished

18:28.780 --> 18:31.910
Tatsumi captured them in the Shadow Vacuum.

18:32.010 --> 18:33.710
I see.

18:33.950 --> 18:36.320
People change depending on who they meet, huh?

18:36.420 --> 18:38.320
Yes...

18:38.420 --> 18:41.750
Those two have quite clearly changed.

18:41.860 --> 18:44.050
Although they still are a handful.

18:47.060 --> 18:50.520
Tatsumi, I feel bad about you
coming over all the time.

18:50.630 --> 18:51.830
Not at all.

18:51.930 --> 18:55.130
It's the least that I can do for you.

18:56.340 --> 18:59.670
Can I ask you one question?

19:00.040 --> 19:01.170
What?

19:02.310 --> 19:06.370
Did it bother you that I rescued you?

19:06.480 --> 19:07.450
Tatsumi...

19:07.550 --> 19:12.510
I didn't want to interfere with your wishes.

19:13.160 --> 19:15.620
That's why I hesitated.

19:15.720 --> 19:20.020
I hesitated about saving you from that hell...

19:23.530 --> 19:25.860
I'm envious of Kurosaki-kun.

19:25.970 --> 19:30.370
Without hesitation,
he was able to act on his own will.

19:31.510 --> 19:33.530
That's not true.

19:34.080 --> 19:37.050
I know how you feel, Tatsumi.

19:38.080 --> 19:40.880
Thank you for saving me.

19:42.250 --> 19:44.880
Thank you, Tatsumi.

19:51.990 --> 19:53.930
Hey, how are things going?

19:54.030 --> 19:55.860
- Hi!
- Here's a little something!

19:55.960 --> 19:58.730
Peach mille feuille in keeping with the season!

19:58.830 --> 19:59.800
Thanks!

19:59.900 --> 20:02.670
It seems like you'll be out soon,
the way you look.

20:02.770 --> 20:06.000
And he's been eating a lot as well.

20:06.110 --> 20:08.470
Huh? Where's Hisoka-san?

20:18.490 --> 20:21.510
You'll catch cold if you stay out there too much.

20:22.520 --> 20:24.250
Tsuzuki...

20:27.600 --> 20:29.590
How's your condition?

20:29.700 --> 20:32.830
You should be more worried about yourself.

20:32.940 --> 20:35.430
You sure had me worried.

20:35.540 --> 20:38.600
As I was swallowed by the flames of Touda

20:38.710 --> 20:41.010
you called me back.

20:41.140 --> 20:43.300
Thank you, Hisoka.

20:43.610 --> 20:45.940
It's so unlike you to say that.

20:54.260 --> 20:58.160
Muraki... is still alive.

20:59.860 --> 21:01.590
I suppose.

21:01.700 --> 21:05.130
He's not one to die so easily.

21:06.370 --> 21:08.130
But that's okay.

21:09.610 --> 21:11.540
As long as he's alive...

21:11.640 --> 21:13.840
I have something to aim for in my life.

21:14.240 --> 21:17.340
One day, I'll exceed him.

21:19.380 --> 21:20.440
Yeah.

21:23.820 --> 21:27.350
I'm sure we can do it, together.

21:48.840 --> 21:52.200
arumikan no marui en o mashikaku ni orinagara

21:48.840 --> 21:52.200
As I square the round edges on the drink

21:52.310 --> 21:55.240
kimi o matsu machikado sa

21:52.310 --> 21:55.240
I wait for you on the street corner

21:55.340 --> 21:58.830
nakami no ekitai wa mou nurukute nomenai kedo

21:55.340 --> 21:58.830
The liquid inside is warm and I can't drink it anymore

21:58.950 --> 22:01.540
shikatanaku motsu ore sa

21:58.950 --> 22:01.540
But what can I do but hold onto to it?

22:01.650 --> 22:08.880
yami no naka de ore o utsusu
garasu keesu ni kazarareta

22:01.650 --> 22:08.880
In the glass case reflecting me in the darkness

22:08.990 --> 22:15.620
ningyou ga sakki kara kowai
kao de ore o miteru

22:08.990 --> 22:15.620
There is a doll that has been scowling at me

22:29.080 --> 22:35.500
ore no fuku kuchibue wa wari
to akarui uta de

22:29.080 --> 22:35.500
The tune I whistle is a bright and cheerful one

22:36.020 --> 22:41.950
zensekai no hitotachi ni
sasagerareta noizu

22:36.020 --> 22:41.950
A little noise dedicated to the people of the world

22:42.720 --> 22:49.060
dare hitori shiru hazu
no nai kono merodi ga

22:42.720 --> 22:49.060
No one could possibly recognize the melody

22:49.810 --> 22:55.210
omae ni wa kikoeru ka? Sayonara da
Love me

22:49.810 --> 22:55.210
But do you hear it?
Good-bye, Love me
